# Spotler Engage Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for Spotler Engage.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for Spotler Engage so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic social media, customer service, or SaaS assumptions. It explains what the product is, who uses it, how it works, which workflows matter, which terminology to use, and what product logic should be preserved.

This is not a Design System Skill. Do not use this Skill for visual styling, component rules, typography, spacing, colours, or layout patterns. Use the separate Spotler Design System Skill or attached design system documentation for those decisions.

---

## Product Summary

Spotler Engage is an integrated webcare and social messaging platform for managing customer conversations, social publishing, media monitoring, WhatsApp messaging, live chat, and team collaboration from one central environment.

It helps teams handle social media comments, private messages, reviews, WhatsApp conversations, live chat messages, and online mentions without switching between channels or missing important messages.

Spotler Engage is designed for organisations that receive large volumes of customer communication across multiple channels and need speed, overview, routing, ownership, collaboration, and consistency.

The product helps teams move from fragmented channel management to one structured webcare operation where conversations can be assigned, tagged, prioritised, monitored, answered, published, and reported on.

---

## Core Problem Spotler Engage Solves

Modern customer communication happens across many public and private channels:

- Social media comments
- Private messages
- Reviews
- WhatsApp
- Live chat
- Chatbots
- News and blogs
- Public online mentions

Without a central platform, organisations face several problems:

- Messages go unanswered
- Teams duplicate work
- It is unclear who should respond
- Sensitive or urgent issues get lost
- Customer response times increase
- Reporting becomes slow or unreliable
- Customers feel ignored
- Crisis communication becomes difficult to coordinate
- Brand reputation signals are missed
- Teams constantly switch between tools and channels

Spotler Engage solves this by bringing webcare, social messaging, publishing, monitoring, and WhatsApp into one collaborative platform.

The goal is to help teams respond faster, maintain a clear overview, assign ownership, coordinate communication, reduce manual work, and stay in control during both day-to-day operations and crisis situations.

---

## Target Users and User Roles

Spotler Engage is primarily used by webcare, communications, marketing, customer service, and reputation management teams.

### Primary users

#### Webcare agent

A webcare agent handles incoming customer conversations across social media, messaging channels, WhatsApp, live chat, reviews, and comments.

Goals:

- Respond quickly and accurately
- Avoid missing messages
- Know which conversations are assigned to them
- See customer or conversation history
- Use internal notes and tags
- Escalate sensitive or complex issues

Typical needs:

- Central inbox
- Configurable inbox views
- Conversation status
- Assignment
- Tags
- Internal notes
- Conversation history
- Channel context

---

#### Webcare team lead

A team lead manages workload, assignments, response quality, and team performance.

Goals:

- Maintain overview of incoming volume
- Assign conversations to the right team members
- Prioritise urgent or sensitive messages
- Monitor response times
- Prevent duplicate work
- Ensure consistent responses

Typical needs:

- Workload insight
- Queue or inbox overview
- Assignment controls
- Status tracking
- Performance reporting
- Team permissions
- Escalation visibility

---

#### Communications manager

A communications manager manages public communication, reputation, crisis response, and coordinated messaging.

Goals:

- Keep communication consistent
- Coordinate public updates
- Monitor online mentions
- Respond to sensitive issues
- Support crisis communication
- Align publishing and webcare

Typical needs:

- Monitoring queries
- Publishing overview
- Conversation prioritisation
- Crisis visibility
- Shared response coordination
- Approval or oversight where needed

---

#### Social media manager

A social media manager creates, schedules, publishes, and manages social media content.

Goals:

- Publish posts across connected social channels
- Coordinate content planning
- Maintain brand and message consistency
- Respond to interactions after publishing
- Use AI assistance for post optimisation

Typical needs:

- Publishing calendar or overview
- Post creation
- Scheduling
- Channel selection
- Post editing
- AI assistant support
- Engagement visibility

---

#### Customer service agent

A customer service agent uses Engage to answer service questions across WhatsApp, social messaging, live chat, and other channels.

Goals:

- Handle enquiries efficiently
- Keep service quality consistent
- Work from one inbox
- See previous conversation history
- Escalate when needed

Typical needs:

- Centralised conversation view
- Contact or conversation history
- Status and ownership
- Quick replies or structured handling
- Team collaboration tools

---

### Secondary users

#### Reputation or crisis manager

A reputation or crisis manager uses monitoring, publishing, and webcare together during sensitive situations.

Goals:

- Detect early signals
- Monitor public discussion
- Prioritise urgent messages
- Coordinate responses
- Maintain control during peak loads

Typical needs:

- Media monitoring
- Query management
- Urgency indicators
- Team coordination
- Publishing and webcare alignment
- Real-time overview

---

#### WhatsApp campaign manager

A WhatsApp campaign manager uses Engage to manage WhatsApp conversations and campaigns.

Goals:

- Run WhatsApp messages or campaigns
- Respond to WhatsApp enquiries
- Keep WhatsApp history in the same environment as other conversations
- Maintain a consistent service experience

Typical needs:

- WhatsApp inbox
- Campaign setup
- Contact-level conversation history
- Status and assignment
- Channel-specific context

---

#### Administrator

An administrator configures channels, permissions, inbox views, workflows, and integrations.

Goals:

- Connect channels
- Manage user access
- Configure inbox views
- Support workflows
- Ensure teams can collaborate safely

Typical needs:

- Channel settings
- Role-based access
- Permission structures
- Routing rules
- Workflow configuration

