## Important Product Objects and Concepts

### Conversation

A customer or audience interaction handled in Engage. A conversation may come from a social comment, direct message, WhatsApp, live chat, review, or chatbot handover.

### Message

An individual incoming or outgoing communication within a conversation.

### Channel

The source or destination of a conversation or post, such as Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, X, TikTok, Threads, live chat, or chatbot.

### Central inbox

The shared environment where conversations from multiple channels are collected and handled.

### Inbox view

A configurable view of conversations based on channel, team, status, assignment, tag, priority, or other criteria.

### Assignment

The process of assigning a conversation to a team member or team.

### Ownership

The person or team responsible for handling a conversation.

### Status

The current handling state of a conversation, such as new, open, assigned, waiting, resolved, or closed.

### Tag

A label used to categorise conversations by topic, urgency, sentiment, department, campaign, or issue type.

### Internal note

A private team note added to a conversation. It is not visible to the customer.

### Public reply

A response sent to the customer or audience through the original channel.

### Routing

The automatic or manual process of directing a conversation to the right inbox, team, or user.

### Priority

An indication of urgency or importance, often used during high-volume or sensitive situations.

### Monitoring query

A structured search query used to track mentions across news, blogs, or social platforms.

### Mention

An online reference to the organisation, brand, campaign, issue, topic, or keyword.

### Publishing

The creation, scheduling, and posting of content to social channels.

### Scheduled post

A post prepared to be published at a specific time.

### Campaign

A coordinated communication effort across one or more channels.

### Crisis situation

A high-pressure or reputationally sensitive moment where message volume, urgency, and risk increase.

### WhatsApp campaign

A structured WhatsApp communication sent or managed through Engage.

### Progressive web app

The mobile-accessible version of Engage used for publishing and webcare on the go.

